      "writtenOn": "2021-03-04T16:33:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this guaranteed to succeed regardless of what profile is passed in? For example, if I were to do:\n\n    mContext.createContextAsUser(UserHandle.of(-5725082))\n\nwould that succeed? Or would it throw? I suppose that since we\u0027re on a binder thread, even if it does throw, the exception will simply be sent back to the caller.\n\nBut given that we keep this UserHandle around and pass it on to the rest of the code (on the handler thread, where we can\u0027t usefully throw any more), it seems like we should validate is somehow. Is there an isValid() method? If not, perhaps we can perform some simplistic validation ourselves like checking that it\u0027s non-negative and \"not too large\"?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9053,
        "startChar": 40,
        "endLine": 9053,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "bc3580809fe36a5e46dedd658463410254021691",
